  "result": "Perfect! All 166 tests pass. I've successfully added customer statement functionality:\n\n**Features added:**\n\n1. **statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)** - generate customer statement\n   - Returns `ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })`\n   - Normalizes customer ID (handles mixed case, spaces)\n   - Returns `CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND` for unknown customer\n   - Filters invoices by:\n     - Customer (by normalized ID)\n     - Status: only `'issued'` or `'partially_paid'`\n     - Issue date: on or before `asOf` (YYYY-MM-DD)\n   - Maps each invoice to: `{ number, issueDate, dueDate, total, due }`\n   - Sorted by `issueDate` ascending\n   - `totalDue`: sum of all invoice `due` amounts\n\n2. **Fixed field preservation**\n   - Updated `issueInvoice` to preserve `terms` and `dueDate`\n   - Updated `recordPayment` to explicitly preserve all invoice fields\n\n**Test coverage (12 new statement tests):**\n- Unknown customer returns error\n- Customer ID normalization\n- Empty statement for customer with no invoices\n- Inclusion of issued invoices\n- Inclusion of partially_paid invoices\n- Exclusion of draft invoices\n- Exclusion of paid invoices\n- Date filtering (before, on, after asOf)\n- Correct sort order by issueDate\n- All required fields present\n- Correct totalDue calculation\n- Customer filtering\n- Partial payment handling\n\nStatement integrates with existing payment system to show balance due per invoice and totals for collection efforts.",
